rules:
  - name: "Template Creation Visibility Bug"
    description: |
      Investigate and fix the issue where newly created templates do not appear in the Templates tab immediately after creation.
    
      exclude:
        - any unrelated module or UI outside of Templates unless directly required
    constraints:
      - Do not touch authentication, routing, or unrelated pages unless a direct dependency is proven.
      - Do not introduce mock data, placeholder logic, or simulated flows.
    goals:
      - Ensure templates are correctly fetched and displayed immediately after creation.
      - Confirm real-time state or API updates are functioning as expected.
      - Fix or implement any required revalidation or state updates.
    enforcement:
      strict: true

  - name: "Phishing Page Creation Visibility Bug"
    description: |
      Investigate and resolve the issue where newly created phishing pages do not show up in the Phishing Pages tab immediately after creation.
    
      exclude:
        - shared utils or global logic unless the issue directly originates there
    constraints:
      - Limit all changes to modules proven to affect Phishing Pages.
      - Do not alter other campaign-related logic unless dependency is confirmed.
      - Maintain production-level quality. No debug code, mocks, or incomplete handlers.
    goals:
      - Ensure phishing pages appear immediately after creation without needing a refresh.
      - Proper state updates, list re-fetching, or optimistic UI rendering.
    enforcement:
      strict: true; 

      🚫 DO NOT modify or touch unrelated files, features, or logic unless 100% necessary for fixing the defined bugs.

✅ Focus only on:

State syncing

API response handling

Reactivity (list refreshing / hook updates)

🛠 If global or shared changes are needed, clearly log and justify them in your explanation.
